    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Question\n\nFrom reading the documentation for the `mini.pair` I get under the impression that something along the\r\n```lua\r\n-- mini.lua\r\nreturn {\r\n\t'nvim-mini/mini.nvim',\r\n\tversion = false,\r\n\tlazy = false,\r\n\r\n\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\trequire('mini.pairs').setup()\r\n\tend,\r\n}\r\n```\r\nShould load the `mini.pairs` module. However that does not happen. Configuring the `mini.pairs` as a standalone plugin does work as expected. Please update the documentation (`mini.nvim` probably) to include the example of how exactly the modules should be configured using the `lazy.nvim`. I am not [alone](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76757832/how-to-configure-lazy-nvim-with-mini-files) finding this confusing. Thanks!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pairs</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From reading the documentation for the <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.pair</code> I get under the impression that something along the</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- mini.lua\nreturn {\n\t'nvim-mini/mini.nvim',\n\tversion = false,\n\tlazy = false,\n\n\tconfig = function()\n\t\trequire('mini.pairs').setup()\n\tend,\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> mini.lua</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> {\n\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>nvim-mini/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">version</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>,\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">lazy</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>,\n\n\t<span class=\"pl-en\">config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.pairs<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n\t<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Should load the <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.pairs</code> module. However that does not happen. Configuring the <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.pairs</code> as a standalone plugin does work as expected. Please update the documentation (<code class=\"notranslate\">mini.nvim</code> probably) to include the example of how exactly the modules should be configured using the <code class=\"notranslate\">lazy.nvim</code>. I am not <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76757832/how-to-configure-lazy-nvim-with-mini-files\" rel=\"nofollow\">alone</a> finding this confusing. Thanks!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pairs\nQuestion\nFrom reading the documentation for the mini.pair I get under the impression that something along the\n-- mini.lua\nreturn {\n\t'nvim-mini/mini.nvim',\n\tversion = false,\n\tlazy = false,\n\n\tconfig = function()\n\t\trequire('mini.pairs').setup()\n\tend,\n}\nShould load the mini.pairs module. However that does not happen. Configuring the mini.pairs as a standalone plugin does work as expected. Please update the documentation (mini.nvim probably) to include the example of how exactly the modules should be configured using the lazy.nvim. I am not alone finding this confusing. Thanks!",
